This file provides high-level installation steps for Greenplum
Database. For detailed installation, configuration and setup 
information see the 'Greenplum Database Installation Guide'
and the 'Greenplum Database Administration Guide'
located in $GPHOME/docs following installation.

For Greenplum Database Single Node Edition (SNE) refer to the 
Quick Start Guide (GPDB-SingleNodeEdition-QuickStart.pdf) for
detailed installation and setup of a single-node Greenplum
Database system.


***********************************************************
RUNNING THE GREENPLUM DATABASE INSTALLER
***********************************************************


1. Open a command-line terminal.

2. Execute the installer using bash:

   /bin/bash greenplum-db-4.0.0.x-<PLATFORM>.bin 

3. When prompted, type 'yes' to accept the license agreement.

4. When prompted, provide an installation path. For example:

   /usr/local/greenplum-db-4.0.0.x


***********************************************************
REQUIRED OS SYSTEM SETTINGS FOR GREENPLUM DATABASE
***********************************************************

These must be set on all Greenplum hosts (master and segments). 
Make sure you restart your system after adding or changing
kernel parameters.


----------------
MAC OS X
----------------
Disable IPv6 network addressing.


Add all of the following to /etc/sysctl.conf:

kern.sysv.shmmax=2147483648
kern.sysv.shmmin=1
kern.sysv.shmmni=64
kern.sysv.shmseg=16
kern.sysv.shmall=524288
kern.maxfiles=65535
kern.maxfilesperproc=65535
net.inet.tcp.msl=60


Add the following to your shell profile file ( such as .bashrc):

ulimit -n 65535


If using DHCP, add the following line to /etc/hostconfig:

HOSTNAME="<your_hostname>"

You would then use this host name when exchanging ssh keys and 
when initializing your Greenplum Database system.


----------------
LINUX
----------------

In /etc/sysctl.conf:

kernel.shmmax = 500000000
kernel.shmmni = 4096
kernel.shmall = 4000000000
kernel.sem = 250 64000 100 512
net.ipv4.tcp_tw_recycle=1 
net.ipv4.tcp_max_syn_backlog=4096 
net.core.netdev_max_backlog=10000
net.ipv4.conf.default.arp_filter=1
net.ipv4.conf.all.arp_filter=1
vm.overcommit_memory=2

In /etc/security/limits.conf:

* soft nofile 65536 
* hard nofile 65536 
* soft nproc 131072
* hard nproc 131072


----------------
SOLARIS 10
----------------

In /etc/project, change the line:

default:3::::

to:

default:3::::project.max-sem-ids=(priv,1024,deny);process.max-file-descriptor=(priv,252144,deny)


***********************************************************
POST INSTALLATION STEPS
***********************************************************

These are the high-level steps to configure and initialize a new 
Greenplum Database instance. For detailed instructions, please 
see the 'Greenplum Database Installation Guide' located in
$GPHOME/docs. 

For Greenplum Database Single Node Edition (SNE) 
refer to the Greenplum Database Single Node Edition 
Quick Start Guide (GPDB-SingleNodeEdition-QuickStart.pdf). 


1. Allocate a 'gpadmin' OS user to own and run your installation.
   This user must exist on all Greenplum hosts.

2. Source the greenplum_path.sh file in your 'gpadmin' user 
   profile (.bashrc) of your master host. This sets the 
   environment variables needed by Greenplum Database.

3. Create your data directory locations on all Greenplum hosts.

4. Use the gpssh-exkeys utility on the master host to exchange 
   SSH keys between all hosts in your Greenplum array. Note that 
   for a single-node configuration you still must exchange 
   ssh keys between the local host and itself.

5. (multi-node configuration only) Use the gpscp and gpssh 
   utilities on the master host to copy and install the 
   Greenplum Database software on all segment hosts.

6. Use the gpinitsystem utility on the master host to 
   initialize and start your Greenplum Database system. This 
   utility requires a configuration file. For example:

   gpinitsystem -c gp_init_config

   A sample multi-node initialization configuration file can 
   be found in $GPHOME/docs/cli_help/gp_init_config_example.

   A sample single-node initialization configuration file can 
   be found in $GPHOME/docs/cli_help/gp_init_singlenode_example.
 
   Edit the appropriate example file to reflect your desired 
   Greenplum Database configuration.

   
   


************************************************
ABOUT YOUR INSTALLATION
************************************************

The Greenplum Database installer installs the following files and 
directories:

* greenplum_path.sh - Greenplum Database environment variables.

* GPDB-LICENSE.txt - Greenplum license agreement.

* bin - Greenplum Database server programs, client programs, and 
        management tools.

* demo - Greenplum Database demonstration programs. 

* docs - Greenplum Database documentation.

* ext - Bundled programs (such as Python) used by some 
        Greenplum Database utilies.

* include - Greenplum Database and PostgreSQL header files.

* lib - Greenplum Database and PostgreSQL library files.

* sbin - Supporting/Internal scripts and programs.

* share - PostgreSQL sample files and templates.



